{"id":"ne1e631c80c","headline":"Argentina's Mercosur Agricultural Share Drops From 42% to 30%","summary":"An agricultural study showed Argentina's share of total Mercosur farm production fell from 42% to 30% between 2000-02 and 2020-22, lagging regional trade partners due to export taxes.","why":"Mercosur is a major global food production bloc. Argentina's relative decline highlights the structural impact of domestic export taxes and productivity differentials against Brazil.","category":"economy","event_type":"macro-data","importance":2,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"Buenos Aires","country":"Argentina","lat":-34.604,"lon":-58.382,"region":"latam"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"Infobae","url":"https://www.infobae.com/economia/2026/11/22/un-estudio-comparo-la-evolucion-de-la-produccion-agraria-de-los-paises-del-mercosur-la-argentina-salio-mal-parada/"},"sources":[{"name":"Infobae","url":"https://www.infobae.com/economia/2026/11/22/un-estudio-comparo-la-evolucion-de-la-produccion-agraria-de-los-paises-del-mercosur-la-argentina-salio-mal-parada/"}],"published_at":"2026-11-22T20:23:33Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-22T21:26:21Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"score":45.7,"content_hash":"c73cefff19af8ece","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/wheat-field-harvest-9738590.jpg","alt":"wheat field harvest (illustration)","credit":"LMX5Fotografie","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/combine-harvester-agriculture-9738590/"}}